## Before you start (5 minutes, no Claude Code needed)

1. Install Node 20+ and the Expo Go app on your phone (iOS or Android).
2. Make an empty folder and open a terminal in it:
   ```
   mkdir badminton-shuffler && cd badminton-shuffler
   git init
   claude
   ```
3. Keep this document open. Paste one prompt at a time.

**Stack being built** (decided for you so Claude Code doesn't wander): Expo + React Native + TypeScript, `expo-router` for the screen flow, Zustand for in-memory state, Vitest for testing the shuffle engine. No database, no backend, no persistence — exactly as you asked.

**Golden rule between phases:** after each phase, run the app on your phone, then commit:
```
git add -A && git commit -m "Phase N: <what it does>"
```
If a phase goes wrong, `git reset --hard HEAD` puts you back to the last working state instead of arguing with the model.

