## Phase 3b — Prove the engine is fair

**Goal:** Don't take the model's word for it. Simulate.

```text
Write Vitest tests in src/engine/__tests__/ that prove the fairness guarantees. Use seeded RNG so every test is deterministic.

Required tests:

1. Capacity: 2 courts + 11 active players → 8 play, 3 sit out. 2 courts + 7 players → 4 play, 3 sit out.
2. Long-run fairness: simulate a full session — 3 courts, 14 players, 20 rounds, recording a random result each round. Assert that at every round boundary the games-played spread across active players is <= 1.
3. No starvation: in the same simulation, assert no player ever sits out 3 rounds in a row.
4. Partner variety: 2 courts, 8 players, 10 rounds. Assert no pair partners a 3rd time before every possible pair has partnered at least once.
5. Late joiner, fair-forward: run 6 rounds with 8 players, then add a 9th. Simulate 10 more rounds. Assert (a) the 9th player's games played over those 10 rounds is within 1 of every other player's games over the same window, and (b) the 9th player never plays more than 2 games more than the group average across any 4-round window (no monopolising).
6. Late joiner keeps the early birds' lead: in the same scenario, assert the newcomer's sessionPoints cannot exceed a player who won every game before they arrived, given equal performance afterwards.
7. Removal mid-session: remove an active player, assert they vanish from future rounds, their stats remain on the leaderboard, and remaining players still satisfy spread <= 1 within 3 rounds.
8. Scoring: a 21-15 win credits both winners identically; both losers get pointsPerLoss; pointsFor/Against are correct; partner and opponent histories increment.
9. Leaderboard ties: construct a tie and assert the tiebreak chain and rank numbering (1, 1, 3) are correct.
10. Purity: assert recordResult and addPlayer do not mutate the input state object.

Run the tests. If any fail, fix the ENGINE, not the test — the tests encode the product promise. Report the final results to me.
```

**Verify before continuing:** all tests green. Ask Claude Code: *"Show me the games-played distribution table from the test 2 simulation"* — eyeball it yourself. Commit.

