## Phase 10 — Hardening

```text
Harden the app against real-world use in a sports hall. Work through this list and report what you found and fixed:

1. Edge cases in the engine — write tests for: fewer than 4 active players mid-session; exactly 4 players and 3 courts (only 1 court usable); all players removed; a player removed then re-added; the session running past its end time; a round generated when every eligible player has identical stats.
2. Guard the UI for each of those: never render a broken round, always explain why a court is empty.
3. Score validation: reject equal scores, negative scores, and warn (but allow) on scores that don't reach the target.
4. Prevent double-submission of a score from a fast double tap.
5. Screen-wake: keep the display awake during an active session (expo-keep-awake) — the organiser's phone sits on a bench between games.
6. Accessibility: labels on all interactive elements, minimum 48pt targets, contrast checked against WCAG AA, reduce-motion respected.
7. Test on the smallest common screen (iPhone SE width, 375pt) and confirm nothing clips or overflows.
8. Add an error boundary that offers "Continue session" rather than losing state on a render crash.
9. Warn before the app can lose state: since nothing is persisted, add a confirmation when navigating back out of an active session.

Then run typecheck, all tests, and lint. Report the results.
```

