## Two decisions worth knowing you're making

**The late joiner rule.** In `fair-forward` mode a newcomer enters the rotation queue level with the *least-played* active player. This is why it does what you want: they get exactly the same number of games as everyone else from that moment on, they never bump other people off courts to "catch up", and because their points genuinely start at zero, whoever showed up on time keeps the lead they earned. The alternative (`catch-up`) is in the config if your group ever prefers it, but fair-forward is the default and the one your requirement describes.

**Nothing is saved.** Closing the app mid-session loses the session, exactly as you specified. Phase 10 adds a confirmation before you can navigate out, and Phase 12's keep-awake setting reduces the risk. If after a few weeks you find you want session recovery, the whole state is one Zustand store — adding AsyncStorage later is roughly a ten-line change, and worth doing as its own phase rather than smuggling it in early.
